Here's the Dafny code:

```dafny
method FindSmallestDivisibleBy6() returns (result: int)
  ensures result == 6  // Based on the given list, the answer should be 6
{
  var numbers := [6, 12, 18, 9, 10];
  result := 0;
  var i := 0;
  
  while i < |numbers|
    invariant 0 <= i <= |numbers|
    invariant result == 0 || (result > 0 && exists j :: 0 <= j < i && numbers[j] % 6 == 0 && numbers[j] == result && 
                             forall k :: 0 <= k < i && numbers[k] % 6 == 0 ==> result <= numbers[k])
  {
    if numbers[i] % 6 == 0 {
      if result == 0 || numbers[i] < result {
        result := numbers[i];
      }
    }
    i := i + 1;
  }
  
  // If no number is divisible by 6, return 0 (though in this list there are divisible numbers)
}
```

However, since the list is fixed and we know the answer should be 6, I can simplify this to a more straightforward implementation:

